and she gave me her E-mail address.

269
00:11:15,490 --> 00:11:20,180
"Jennifer@not-even-if-you-were- the-last-guy-on-earth.loser""

270
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:22,730
What?

271
00:11:22,730 --> 00:11:24,240
I'm sorry, Raj.

272
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:26,330
Why can't I find someone?

273
00:11:26,330 --> 00:11:28,260
I'm smart, I've got a cool job,

274
00:11:28,260 --> 00:11:30,340
and my naturally bronzed complexion means

275
00:11:30,340 --> 00:11:33,470
I can pull off mustard yellow in a way most guys can't.

276
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:36,460
Oh, honey, it's not you, it's them.

277
00:11:36,460 --> 00:11:38,160
No, it's not.

278
00:11:38,160 --> 00:11:40,460
She was too beautiful for me.

279
00:11:40,460 --> 00:11:43,040
- Why would you say that? - It's true.

280
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:44,970
I'm always attracted to women I can't have.

281
00:11:44,970 --> 00:11:46,490
I do it all the time.

282
00:11:46,490 --> 00:11:48,730
I did the same thing with the two of you.

283
00:11:49,450 --> 00:11:50,450
The two of them?

284
00:11:50,450 --> 00:11:51,810
I don't understand.

285
00:11:53,040 --> 00:11:56,570
Well, uh, there was a time when I had a thing for Penny,

286
00:11:56,580 --> 00:11:58,090
and I thought she was into me, too,

287
00:11:58,090 --> 00:11:59,420
because she got drunk and naked

288
00:11:59,430 --> 00:12:00,680
and climbed into bed with me.

289
00:12:00,780 --> 00:12:03,730
But apparently I misread those signals.

290
00:12:06,090 --> 00:12:08,030
And you liked Bernadette also?

291
00:12:08,030 --> 00:12:10,100
That was before Penny.

292
00:12:10,100 --> 00:12:11,450
I make it a rule to only fall for

293
00:12:11,450 --> 00:12:14,280
one of my friends' girlfriends at a time.

294
00:12:14,790 --> 00:12:17,360
I'm very old-fashioned that way.

295
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:20,130
So at, uh, some point,

296
00:12:20,130 --> 00:12:23,330
you probably had a thing for me, too.

297
00:12:25,010 --> 00:12:26,840
No, not really.

298
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:33,060
Oh, come on, Raj, not even a little bit?

299
00:12:33,060 --> 00:12:35,260
Not that I can think of.

300
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:39,150
Think harder.

301
00:12:40,590 --> 00:12:41,880
Nope.

302
00:12:41,880 --> 00:12:44,110
I guess the heart wants what the heart wants.

303
00:12:44,110 --> 00:12:45,330
Or in this case, doesn't.

304
00:12:45,330 --> 00:12:47,410
I mean, at all.

305
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:52,530
What?

306
00:12:54,670 --> 00:12:56,740
* Ye who now will bless the poor *

307
00:12:56,740 --> 00:13:00,280
* Shall yourselves find blessing *

308
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:05,140
Done?

309
00:13:05,140 --> 00:13:07,430
I think the word you're looking for is "bravo."

310
00:13:08,900 --> 00:13:11,350
Okay, you leave the room and find yourself

311
00:13:11,350 --> 00:13:13,600
standing before a pool of melted snowmen.

312
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:15,160
Melted snowmen?

313
00:13:15,160 --> 00:13:17,310
Are there carrots and lumps of coal in the water?

314
00:13:17,310 --> 00:13:18,920
I don't know. What's the difference?

315
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:20,640
It's a game of the imagination, Leonard.

316
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:22,520
- Paint a picture. - Fine.

317
00:13:22,520 --> 00:13:24,060
You leave the room and find yourself

318
00:13:24,060 --> 00:13:25,840
standing before a pool of melted snowmen.

319
00:13:25,840 --> 00:13:27,760
There are carrots and lumps of coal in the water.

320
00:13:27,760 --> 00:13:30,940
Do we know what happened to the top hats and the corncob pipes?

321
00:13:31,270 --> 00:13:32,420
You see those, too.

322
00:13:32,420 --> 00:13:35,270
Oh, it's like I'm really there.

323
00:13:37,440 --> 00:13:40,940
I gotta tell you, this-this is the most holiday fun I've had

324
00:13:40,950 --> 00:13:44,110
since my therapist changed my anxiety medication

325
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:46,630
and I stopped caring about the blood in my stool.

326
00:13:50,060 --> 00:13:51,680
Good story.

327
00:13:52,620 --> 00:13:53,640
What are you drinking there?

328
00:13:53,640 --> 00:13:54,830
Little eggnog?

329
00:13:54,830 --> 00:13:55,760
Yes.

330
00:13:55,760 --> 00:13:56,730
What, is there a problem?

331
00:13:56,730 --> 00:14:00,140
No, it's nice to see you enjoying a holiday beverage.

332
00:14:00,140 --> 00:14:01,370
Pretty Christmasy.

333
00:14:01,370 --> 00:14:03,950
Since when is eggnog a Christmas drink?

334
00:14:04,250 --> 00:14:06,810
Eggs are available all year 'round.

335
00:14:06,810 --> 00:14:09,410
I've been known to enjoy this poolside.

336
00:14:10,230 --> 00:14:11,720
Come on, Sheldon.

337
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:14,330
You know all the Christmas stories, and the carols,

338
00:14:14,330 --> 00:14:16,360
you've got an eggnog mustache going on there.

339
00:14:16,370 --> 00:14:17,650
Just admit it.

340
00:14:17,650 --> 00:14:19,250
You're getting a little Yuletide spirit.

341
00:14:19,250 --> 00:14:20,560
Oh, don't be silly.

342
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:23,650
Christmas is a bunch of baloney created by the tinsel industry.

343
00:14:24,510 --> 00:14:26,490
Why is this so important to you?

344
00:14:26,490 --> 00:14:28,590
Honestly, because I had enough crappy Christmases as a kid

345
00:14:28,590 --> 00:14:30,880
and I'm tired of you sucking the joy out of them now.

346
00:14:31,350 --> 00:14:32,580
What was so bad about them?

347
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:35,430
I grew up in a house full of crazy academics.

348
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:37,640
Instead of leaving Santa milk and cookies,

349
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:39,940
we had to leave him a research paper.

350
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:43,100
And in the morning, you could tell he'd been there

351
00:14:43,100 --> 00:14:45,180
because the paper would be graded.

352
00:14:46,740 --> 00:14:47,870
No wonder you love Christmas.

353
00:14:47,870 --> 00:14:49,960
That sounds amazing.

354
00:14:50,630 --> 00:14:52,230
It wasn't amazing.

355
00:14:52,230 --> 00:14:55,050
I got a C-minus four years in a row.

356
00:14:55,050 --> 00:14:56,740
Yeah, I'm familiar with your work.

357
00:14:56,740 --> 00:14:58,610
C-minus was your gift.

358
00:15:02,050 --> 00:15:03,980
Amy, I'm really sorry.

359
00:15:03,980 --> 00:15:05,840
I didn't mean to upset you.

360
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:06,760
It's fine.

361
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:09,720
I'm used to being the girl who never gets looked at twice.

362
00:15:09,720 --> 00:15:11,960
I didn't have my first kiss till I was 22,

363
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:15,280
and the guy only did it so I'd give him back his insulin.

364
00:15:18,190 --> 00:15:21,870
Sometimes the pancreas wants what the pancreas wants.

365
00:15:22,870 --> 00:15:23,670
Forget it.

366
00:15:23,670 --> 00:15:25,650
I don't expect you guys to understand.

367
00:15:25,650 --> 00:15:27,080
I understand.

368
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:28,970
In seventh grade, I played Spin the Bottle

369
00:15:28,970 --> 00:15:30,610
and it landed on Alina Shankar.

370
00:15:30,610 --> 00:15:31,700
She said if I came near her,

371
00:15:31,700 --> 00:15:34,890
she would break the bottle and cut me.

372
00:15:34,890 --> 00:15:36,530
You think that's bad?

373
00:15:36,530 --> 00:15:38,260
In college, I passed out at a frat party

374
00:15:38,260 --> 00:15:41,360
and woke up with more clothes on.

375
00:15:45,670 --> 00:15:47,040
Sometimes I get so lonely,

376
00:15:47,040 --> 00:15:49,320
I sit on my left hand until it goes numb,

377
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:50,640
then I put it in my right hand

378
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:53,920
and pretend I'm holding hands with another person.

379
00:15:54,680 --> 00:15:56,660
I do that, too.

380
00:15:57,050 --> 00:15:59,610
Sometimes the left hand tries to cop a feel.

381
00:16:01,050 --> 00:16:02,850
And I let it.

382
00:16:05,630 --> 00:16:08,140
It's kind of nice to talk to someone who understands

383
00:16:08,140 --> 00:16:09,940
what it feels like to be alone.

384
00:16:09,950 --> 00:16:11,460
It is, isn't it?

385
00:16:11,460 --> 00:16:12,760
But you're not alone anymore.

386
00:16:12,760 --> 00:16:15,020
- Now you've got Sheldon. - I do.

387
00:16:15,020 --> 00:16:18,330
And don't worry, someday you'll have somebody, too.

388
00:16:18,330 --> 00:16:19,540
Thank you.

389
00:16:19,540 --> 00:16:23,210
I hope she's half as lovely and amazing as you are.

390
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,920
Thank you, Rajesh.

391
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:29,420
He wants me, I'm good. We can go now.

392
00:16:31,650 --> 00:16:32,550
Damn it.

393
00:16:32,550 --> 00:16:33,510
What?

394
00:16:33,510 --> 00:16:35,750
Now that I know she doesn't like me,

395
00:16:35,750 --> 00:16:37,530
I'm kind of into her.

396
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:40,670
All right.

397
00:16:40,670 --> 00:16:44,870
I think I cracked the code to lower the drawbridge.

398
00:16:44,870 --> 00:16:46,660
Great. Let's do it.

399
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:54,690
The drawbridge is lowering.

400
00:17:01,030 --> 00:17:02,530
My carpal tunnel's acting up.

401
00:17:02,530 --> 00:17:03,680
Play through the pain!

402
00:17:15,280 --> 00:17:17,230
You did it! The drawbridge is down.

403
00:17:17,230 --> 00:17:18,520
You cross the chasm

404
00:17:18,520 --> 00:17:21,340
and find yourself in a small dungeon room.

405
00:17:21,340 --> 00:17:24,080
And in the corner, chained to the wall,

406
00:17:24,080 --> 00:17:26,660
you see a bloodied and beaten Santa Claus.

407
00:17:26,660 --> 00:17:30,110
He says, "Ho, ho, help me."

408
00:17:30,770 --> 00:17:33,030
Yes, we found Santa!

409
00:17:33,030 --> 00:17:35,030
Christmas is saved!

410
00:17:35,030 --> 00:17:37,990
Don't ever tell my mother I said that.

411
00:17:38,530 --> 00:17:40,400
I take out my skeleton key

412
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:42,200
and run to Santa to unchain him.

413
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:46,180
But first, I cast a spell of paralysis on Stuart and Howard.

414
00:17:46,180 --> 00:17:46,920
What are you doing?

415
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:49,060
You can't talk; you're paralyzed.

416
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:52,790
I get right up in Santa's big, fat face and say...

417
00:17:52,790 --> 00:17:54,670
Well, well, well,

418
00:17:54,670 --> 00:17:57,580
Jolly old Saint Nick, we meet again.

419
00:17:57,580 --> 00:17:59,070
Yeah, I believe the last time we spoke

420
00:17:59,070 --> 00:18:02,140
was in the Baybrook Mall in Galveston, Texas,

421
00:18:02,140 --> 00:18:04,390
when I was five years old, isn't that right?

422
00:18:04,390 --> 00:18:06,000
Uh, okay.

423
00:18:06,610 --> 00:18:07,980
My mother dragged me there

424
00:18:07,980 --> 00:18:09,590
and she plopped me down on your lap

425
00:18:09,590 --> 00:18:12,160
and you asked me what I wanted for Christmas.

426
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:14,300
And I told you "My Pop-Pop,"

427
00:18:14,300 --> 00:18:16,850
because that was the year my grandfather died.

428
00:18:16,850 --> 00:18:20,020
I missed him and I wanted him back.

429
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:22,840
This is weird, right?

430
00:18:25,530 --> 00:18:27,320
Pop-Pop was the only one in my family

431
00:18:27,320 --> 00:18:29,690
who encouraged me to pursue science.

432
00:18:29,690 --> 00:18:32,040
But you didn't bring him back, did you?

433
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:34,810
Instead, I got Lincoln Logs.

434
00:18:34,810 --> 00:18:38,390
Well, you can build a lot of neat things out of Lincoln Logs,

435
00:18:38,390 --> 00:18:40,620
but Pop-Pop ain't one of 'em.

436
00:18:40,620 --> 00:18:43,880
And now you're here asking me for something--

437
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:45,100
to save you.

438
00:18:45,100 --> 00:18:47,510
Well, sorry, Mr. Kringle,

439
00:18:47,510 --> 00:18:49,210
but today's not your day.

440
00:18:49,210 --> 00:18:51,010
I'm leaving you here to rot,

441
00:18:51,010 --> 00:18:53,650
and I hope the ogres feast on your bones.

442
00:18:53,650 --> 00:18:55,370
I take the skeleton key,

443
00:18:55,370 --> 00:18:57,220
and I toss it into the chasm,

444
00:18:57,220 --> 00:18:58,950
and on the way out, I give Santa

445
00:18:58,950 --> 00:19:01,650
a swift kick in his bowl full of jelly!

446
00:19:04,270 --> 00:19:05,880
Okay.

447
00:19:05,880 --> 00:19:09,160
So Wolowitz and Stuart are paralyzed, Santa's dead,

448
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:12,000
and I picked this over having sex with my girlfriend.

449
00:19:28,160 --> 00:19:29,390
Santa?

450
00:19:29,390 --> 00:19:33,150
Oh, hello, Sheldon.

451
00:19:33,150 --> 00:19:35,750
You should be asleep.

452
00:19:35,750 --> 00:19:38,290
Well, then, you shouldn't have jingle bells on your boots.

453
00:19:40,330 --> 00:19:42,340
I've been wanting to talk to you.

454
00:19:42,340 --> 00:19:46,910
I'm sorry I disappointed you when you were a little boy.

455
00:19:48,410 --> 00:19:50,860
I-I can do a lot of magical things,

456
00:19:50,860 --> 00:19:52,570
but unfortunately

457
00:19:52,580 --> 00:19:55,920
bringing your Pop-Pop back isn't one of them.

458
00:19:57,110 --> 00:19:58,670
I understand.

459
00:19:58,670 --> 00:20:02,230
But I-I do have something special for you.

460
00:20:02,840 --> 00:20:04,870
Close your eyes.

461
00:20:06,670 --> 00:20:09,130
Oh, I hope it's a train.

462
00:20:09,140 --> 00:20:12,290
Oh, it's better than a train.

463
00:20:12,290 --> 00:20:15,520
Two trains?

464
00:20:15,530 --> 00:20:17,240
Better.

465
00:20:17,250 --> 00:20:19,420
I'm getting three trains.

466
00:20:21,230 --> 00:20:22,840
Okay, open 'em.

467
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:29,090
This is for leaving me in the dungeon

468
00:20:29,090 --> 00:20:31,580
to be eaten alive by ogres!

469
00:20:31,590 --> 00:20:32,900
Wait, uh, uh, hang on.

470
00:20:32,910 --> 00:20:34,030
I-In my defense...

471
00:20:34,350 --> 00:20:36,830
Ho, ho, ho, ya big dork!

